Definition:
Testing the changes to an operational system includes both evaluating the success of the implementation of the change and the checking for possible regressions in parts of the system that remain unchanged. The scope of maintenance testing typically depends on: 
• the degree of risk of the change; 
• the size of the existing system; 
• the size of the change.

It is concerned with providing an awareness of product risk to focus the test effort in a way that minimizes the residual level of risk. Risk analysis consists of: 
• Risk identification – generating a comprehensive list of risks; 
• Risk assessment – categorization of identified risks, determining their risk likelihood, risk impact and risk level, prioritizing, and proposing ways to handle them.
